{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","$id":"https://specs.makemind.com/mcp_ui_dsl/1.4/page.schema.json","title":"MCP UI DSL 1.4 — PageDefinition","type":"object","properties":{"type":{"enum":["page","screen"],"description":"Discriminator. `screen` is a legacy alias accepted for backward compatibility (§17.3.5)."},"version":{"$ref":"#/$defs/SemverLike"},"title":{"type":"string"},"content":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Widget"},"themeOverride":{"$ref":"https://specs.makemind.com/mcp_ui_dsl/1.4/theme.schema.json"},"state":{"$ref":"#/$defs/StateBlock"},"lifecycle":{"$ref":"#/$defs/LifecycleHooks"},"onInit":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onReady":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onMount":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onPause":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onResume":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onUnmount":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onDestroy":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"validation":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ValidationConfig"},"permissions":{"$ref":"#/$defs/PermissionDeclaration"},"channels":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ChannelMap"}},"required":["type","content"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Single-screen page definition per docs/01_Core_Concepts.md §1.3. Widget and action sub-trees are validated by widgets.schema.json — left permissive here so this schema is self-contained.","$defs":{"Action":{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string"}},"required":["type"],"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Action per docs/04_Actions.md. Discriminator `type`; per-type fields validated by widgets.schema.json's Action def."},"ActionOrList":{"oneOf":[{"$ref":"#/$defs/Action"},{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Action"}}]},"Alignment":{"oneOf":[{"enum":["topStart","topLeft","topCenter","topEnd","topRight","centerStart","centerLeft","center","centerEnd","centerRight","bottomStart","bottomLeft","bottomCenter","bottomEnd","bottomRight"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"x":{"type":"number","minimum":-1,"maximum":1},"y":{"type":"number","minimum":-1,"maximum":1}},"required":["x","y"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}],"description":"2D alignment within a rectangle. Token names are **directional**\n(RTL-aware) per Material 3:\n\n- `topStart` — top corner on the leading edge (top-left in LTR,\n  top-right in RTL).\n- `topEnd` — top corner on the trailing edge.\n- `centerStart` / `centerEnd`, `bottomStart` / `bottomEnd` — same\n  convention on the middle / bottom rows.\n- `topCenter`, `center`, `bottomCenter` — neutral on the cross\n  axis.\n\nObject form `{x, y}` is a numeric pair where each axis runs from\n-1 (start) through 0 (center) to 1 (end). The numeric form\nsupports any point inside or outside the rectangle.\n\nCross-schema canonical for any \"2D rectangle alignment\" use —\nchild placement (`box.alignment`, `align.alignment`,\n`stack.alignment`), gradient endpoints (`Gradient.begin/end`),\nimage fit (`BackgroundImage.alignment`)."},"AnimationCurve":{"enum":["linear","easeIn","easeOut","easeInOut","standard","standardAccelerate","standardDecelerate","emphasized","emphasizedAccelerate","emphasizedDecelerate","bounceIn","bounceOut"],"description":"Easing curve applied to an animation's progress. Eleven canonical\nvalues cover the M3-recommended palette plus the CSS-familiar\nbasics:\n\n- **CSS-familiar** — `linear`, `easeIn`, `easeOut`, `easeInOut`.\n- **M3 standard** — `standard`, `standardAccelerate`,\n  `standardDecelerate`. Used for everyday transitions; minimal\n  overshoot, clean cubic.\n- **M3 emphasized** — `emphasized`, `emphasizedAccelerate`,\n  `emphasizedDecelerate`. Used for hero / page transitions; more\n  dramatic acceleration profile.\n- **Bounce** — `bounceIn`, `bounceOut`. For attention / alert\n  micro-interactions.\n\nCross-schema canonical for `animatedContainer.curve`,\n`animatedOpacity.curve`, RouteTransition, scrollAnimated easing,\nand any future implicit-animation widget. Matches the M3 motion\nspec's named tokens 1:1 so theme-level motion overrides stay\nvendor-neutral."},"AssetRef":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*:|assets/)"},{"type":"object","properties":{"uri":{"type":"string","description":"Resource uri read through MCP `resources/read` on the resolved origin."},"origin":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Origin"}},"required":["uri"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Reference to an asset (image, font, audio, video, SVG, …).\n\nAn asset reference takes one of three shapes: a **scheme-prefixed\nstring**, an **object** naming a resource and the origin that serves\nit, or a **binding** that resolves to either at render time.\n\n## Known schemes\n\nA runtime dispatches the right loader by prefix:\n\n- `bundle://<path>` — asset packaged inside the active bundle. Inside\n  an embedded subtree this is the *embedded* document's bundle, not\n  the embedder's (`06_Runtime_Contract.md` §6.11.3).\n- `https://<url>` / `http://<url>` — fetched over the network and\n  cached on first render.\n- `data:<mime>;base64,<payload>` (or `data:<mime>,<urlencoded>`) —\n  inline bytes carried in the DSL itself. The only form that needs no\n  I/O capability at all, and so the one a constrained host can always\n  render.\n- `assets/<path>` — Flutter-style local asset path declared in the\n  consumer app's pubspec asset list (used by host integrations that\n  ship icon SVGs alongside the runtime).\n- `client://<channel>/<id>` — resource served by the client / host\n  process via an MCP client-extension channel (`08_Client_Extensions.md`\n  §8.3). This is how a document reaches the *host's* own files —\n  `client://file/…`, `client://workspace/…` — rather than the server's.\n\n**This list is open, not closed.** The pattern admits any RFC 3986\nscheme so a host may serve forms this document does not name, exactly\nas `Origin` admits sources beyond `connection`. A runtime that meets a\nscheme it does not implement MUST fail visibly per §6.12 rather than\nreject the document — an author naming a scheme this runtime lacks has\nwritten a valid document that this runtime cannot fully render, which\nis not the same as an invalid document.\n\n## Object form — an asset served by an origin\n\n```json\n{ \"uri\": \"file:///reports/2026-q2.pdf\", \"origin\": { \"connection\": \"{{ deviceId }}\" } }\n```\n\n`uri` is read through MCP `resources/read` on the named origin. No new\nscheme is minted for \"the server's own asset\": MCP already reads an\narbitrary resource uri and returns text or base64 `blob`, so a server\npublishes assets the same way it publishes anything else.\n\n`origin` is the `Origin` primitive, so addressing an asset and\naddressing a definition use one vocabulary. Omitted, the asset resolves\nagainst the **ambient origin** — the origin of the definition that\ndeclares it (§6.11.3), never the embedder's.\n\nThe object form is what lets an asset stay *out* of application state.\nA server with room can publish a resource uri and let the runtime pull\nthe bytes; a server without room can inline the same asset as a `data:`\nstring. Both are valid, and which one a server chooses is its own\ndecision — the DSL does not force a transport on it.\n\n## Support is declared, not assumed\n\nRuntimes declare which schemes they resolve (§6.12, §18.9). Nothing\nhere requires a runtime to implement all of them; it requires a runtime\nto be honest about which it does, and to route the rest to the\nconsumer's declared fallback instead of a blank box or a placeholder\nbearing an implementation detail.\n\nUsed cross-schema by `app` (splash · publisher logos · font assets),\n`page`/widgets (image · icon · avatar · lottieAnimation ·\nBackgroundImage · mediaPlayer · rive · lightbox), and `theme` (font\nasset registration). Lives under `configs/_primitive/` for that reason."},"BackgroundImage":{"type":"object","properties":{"image":{"$ref":"#/$defs/AssetRef"},"fit":{"enum":["fill","contain","cover","fitWidth","fitHeight","none","scaleDown"],"default":"cover"},"alignment":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Alignment"},"opacity":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1},"colorFilter":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color"},"blendMode":{"enum":["srcIn","color","screen","overlay","multiply"],"default":"srcIn","description":"Curated subset of blend modes covering the common tinting use cases (`srcIn` for solid tint, `color` for hue swap, `screen`/`overlay`/`multiply` for atmosphere)."}},"required":["color"],"additionalProperties":false},"repeat":{"enum":["noRepeat","repeat","repeatX","repeatY"],"default":"noRepeat"}},"required":["image"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Image fill behind a box's content. `image` accepts the same forms as\nthe `image` widget's `src` (`bundle://`, `https?://`, `data:`,\n`client://`). `fit` and `alignment` mirror the `image` widget's\nsemantics. `opacity` applies an alpha multiplier; `colorFilter`\ncomposites a tint via the named blend mode. `repeat` controls\ntiling behaviour outside the image's natural bounds."},"Binding":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\{\\{.*\\}\\}$","description":"Binding-expression string of the form `\"{{...}}\"`. Authors may\nsubstitute any primitive value with a binding so the runtime\nresolves the value at render time. Used as an alternative branch\nin primitives that otherwise expect a specific structural shape\n(AssetRef, Dimension, BorderRadius, Alignment, …)."},"BorderRadius":{"oneOf":[{"type":"number","minimum":0},{"type":"object","properties":{"topStart":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"topEnd":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"bottomStart":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"bottomEnd":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"all":{"type":"number","minimum":0}},"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Per-corner radius value. A bare number applies uniformly to all\nfour corners; the object form lets each corner take an independent\nradius. `all` is a shorthand for setting every corner at once and\nis overridden by individual corner keys.\n\nCorner names are **directional** (RTL-aware) per Material 3:\n\n- `topStart` — top corner on the leading edge (top-left in LTR,\n  top-right in RTL).\n- `topEnd` — top corner on the trailing edge.\n- `bottomStart` / `bottomEnd` — same convention on the bottom row.\n\nThis is the cross-schema canonical for any \"per-corner radius\"\nshape — referenced by `theme.Shape` (M3 shape token sizes) and by\nthe `BoxDecoration.borderRadius` widget property."},"ChannelDefinition":{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","description":"Channel type — `client.watchFile`, `client.watchDirectory`, `client.systemMonitor`, `client.poll`, `client.websocket`, `client.mcpStream` per §8.6.2."},"url":{"type":"string"},"tool":{"type":"string"},"params":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true},"binding":{"type":"string"},"lifecycle":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ChannelLifecycle"},"onMessage":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onConnect":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onDisconnect":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onError":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"}},"required":["type"],"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Long-lived bidirectional stream per docs/08_Client_Extensions.md §8.6."},"ChannelLifecycle":{"type":"object","properties":{"autoStart":{"type":"boolean","default":false},"autoDispose":{"type":"boolean","default":false},"restartOnError":{"type":"boolean","default":false},"maxRestarts":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"default":3},"restartDelay":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"default":1000},"restartBackoff":{"enum":["fixed","linear","exponential"],"default":"fixed"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Channel lifecycle config per docs/08_Client_Extensions.md §8.6.5."},"ChannelMap":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ChannelDefinition"}},"Color":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^#([0-9a-fA-F]{3}|[0-9a-fA-F]{6}|[0-9a-fA-F]{8})$","description":"Hex — `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, or `#AARRGGBB` (alpha first)."},{"description":"Material 3 scheme slot (§5.3) — adapts to light / dark mode.","enum":["primary","onPrimary","primaryContainer","onPrimaryContainer","secondary","onSecondary","secondaryContainer","onSecondaryContainer","tertiary","onTertiary","tertiaryContainer","onTertiaryContainer","error","onError","errorContainer","onErrorContainer","surface","onSurface","onSurfaceVariant","surfaceTint","surfaceBright","surfaceDim","surfaceContainerLowest","surfaceContainerLow","surfaceContainer","surfaceContainerHigh","surfaceContainerHighest","outline","outlineVariant","inverseSurface","onInverseSurface","inverseOnSurface","background","onBackground","surfaceVariant","inversePrimary","scrim","shadow","success","onSuccess","warning","onWarning","info","onInfo","divider","foreground","textOnPrimary","textOnSecondary","textOnBackground","textOnSurface","textOnError"],"x-legacy":["divider","foreground","textOnPrimary","textOnSecondary","textOnBackground","textOnSurface","textOnError"],"x-legacy-note":"Pre-M3 slot names (§17.3). Accepted so documents written before §5.3.1's roles keep loading and painting; §5.3.1 lists what to write now."},{"type":"string","pattern":"^([Rr][Ee][Dd]|[Bb][Ll][Uu][Ee]|[Gg][Rr][Ee][Ee][Nn]|[Yy][Ee][Ll][Ll][Oo][Ww]|[Oo][Rr][Aa][Nn][Gg][Ee]|[Pp][Uu][Rr][Pp][Ll][Ee]|[Bb][Ll][Aa][Cc][Kk]|[Ww][Hh][Ii][Tt][Ee]|[Gg][Rr][Ee][Yy]|[Gg][Rr][Aa][Yy])$","description":"CSS basic color name. Spelled as a character class per\nletter because JSON Schema regexes are ECMA-262, which has no\ninline `(?i:)` flag — writing one makes the whole branch\nunconstrained instead of case-insensitive, and it accepted every\nstring."},{"type":"string","pattern":"^[Rr][Gg][Bb][Aa]? *\\( *[0-9]{1,3} *, *[0-9]{1,3} *, *[0-9]{1,3} *(, *([01]|[01]?[.][0-9]+) *)?\\) *$","description":"Functional notation — `rgb(r, g, b)` or `rgba(r, g, b, a)`,\nchannels 0-255 and alpha 0-1. §5.3.4 rates it SHOULD, below hex:\nit carries no alpha in the three-channel form and does not adapt\nto light / dark mode the way a scheme slot does."},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}],"description":"A color value. Three spellings, all accepted wherever a color is\nexpected:\n\n- **Hex** — `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, or `#AARRGGBB`. The 8-digit form puts\n  alpha **first**, matching the runtime's parse order.\n- **Theme scheme slot** — a bare Material 3 role name from §5.3.1\n  (`primary`, `onSurfaceVariant`, `error`, …), the three semantic pairs\n  this spec adds (`success`, `warning`, `info` and their `on*`), and the\n  four legacy spellings §5.3.1 keeps (`background`, `onBackground`,\n  `surfaceVariant`, `inverseOnSurface`).\n  Resolved against the active theme, so it follows light / dark mode.\n  This is the preferred form: it is the only one that adapts.\n- **CSS basic name** — the ten colors a document can name without a\n  theme (`red`, `blue`, `green`, `yellow`, `orange`, `purple`,\n  `black`, `white`, `grey`/`gray`). Matched case-insensitively.\n- **Functional** — `rgb(r, g, b)` / `rgba(r, g, b, a)`. §5.3.4 rates\n  this SHOULD where hex is MUST; it is accepted so that a theme\n  written in that notation validates, but it adapts to neither mode\n  nor palette.\n\nBindings are accepted in all three positions.\n\nA bare word that is neither a scheme slot nor a basic name is **not**\na color: the runtime resolves it to null and the widget falls back to\nits default. Validators reject it rather than let it render as a\nsilent default."},"DefinitionSource":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\{\\{.*\\}\\}$","description":"Binding to a definition held in state (since v1.4)."},{"type":"string","description":"Resource URI on the current origin, e.g. `ui://pages/main`."},{"type":"object","description":"Qualified reference to a definition on another origin (since v1.4).","properties":{"$ref":{"type":"string","description":"Resource URI to read from the named origin."},"from":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Origin"}},"required":["$ref"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","description":"Inline PageDefinition or WidgetDefinition."}],"description":"Where a definition comes from. Four forms: an inline definition, a resource\nURI on the current origin, a qualified `{ $ref, from }` reference to another\norigin, or a binding to a definition already held in state.\n\nOmitting `from` means the current origin, so every pre-1.4 document keeps its\nexact meaning. Naming an origin makes that origin ambient for the resolved\nsubtree — its tool calls, resource reads, state, storage and permissions all\nscope to it. See `01_Core_Concepts.md` §1.9 and `07_Security.md` §7.10.\n\nAccepted wherever `RouteValue` is accepted (§1.2.1) and as the `source` of the\n`view` widget (§2.13.1)."},"Dimension":{"oneOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"oneOf":[{"type":"number"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}]},"unit":{"type":"string"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Numeric size — accepts a plain `number` (logical pixels) OR the\nlegacy MCP UI DSL v1.0 `{value, unit}` object form. The `unit`\nfield is informational; the runtime treats every dimension as\nlogical pixels. `value` may itself be a binding: a bar whose width\ncomes from data writes `{\"value\": \"{{item.ratio}}\", \"unit\": \"percent\"}`,\nand that is the whole point of the object form."},"EdgeInsets":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"number"},"unit":{"type":"string"}},"required":["value"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"all":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"horizontal":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"vertical":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"top":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"right":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"bottom":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"left":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"}}},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Space around or inside a box. Four spellings, all accepted wherever insets\nare expected:\n\n- **Number** — one value applied to every edge.\n- **`{value, unit}`** — the legacy v1.0 dimension object; `unit` is\n  informational and the runtime treats every inset as logical pixels.\n- **Edge map** — `{all}` for every edge, `{horizontal, vertical}` for the\n  two axes, or `{top, right, bottom, left}` for individual edges. Each entry\n  is a `Dimension`, so one edge may be bound while its neighbours are\n  literal: `{ \"left\": \"{{sidebar.width}}\", \"top\": 8 }`.\n- **Binding** — resolves to any of the above at render time.\n\nA bare word is not an inset: the runtime resolves it to null and the widget\nfalls back to no padding, so validators reject it rather than let it render\nas a silent zero."},"Gradient":{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"enum":["linear","radial","sweep"]},"colors":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color"},"minItems":2},"stops":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1}},"begin":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Alignment"},"end":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Alignment"},"center":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Alignment"},"radius":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"startAngle":{"type":"number"},"endAngle":{"type":"number"},"tileMode":{"enum":["clamp","repeated","mirror"],"default":"clamp"}},"required":["type","colors"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Multi-stop gradient fill. Selected by `type`:\n\n- `linear` — straight axis from `begin` (default `centerLeft`) to\n  `end` (default `centerRight`).\n- `radial` — circular gradient out from `center` (default `center`)\n  to `radius` (default `0.5`, expressed as a fraction of the\n  bounding rectangle's longest side).\n- `sweep` — angular gradient around `center`, swept from\n  `startAngle` (default `0`) to `endAngle` (default `2π`) in\n  radians.\n\n`colors` lists at least two color values; `stops` (optional) places\neach color at a position in `[0, 1]`. `tileMode` controls behaviour\npast the gradient extents."},"IconRef":{"$comment":"anyOf, not oneOf: the name branch is an unconstrained string, so a binding expression matches both it and the Binding branch. `oneOf` reads that legitimate value as a violation — the same reason the Widget union uses anyOf.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","description":"Icon name, or an AssetRef string (scheme-prefixed, or an `assets/` path)."},{"type":"object","properties":{"codepoint":{"type":"integer"},"fontFamily":{"type":"string"},"fontPackage":{"type":"string"}},"required":["codepoint"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"uri":{"type":"string","description":"Resource uri read through MCP `resources/read` on the resolved origin."},"origin":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Origin"}},"required":["uri"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Reference to an icon. Three forms, all accepted anywhere an icon is\ntaken — the `icon` widget and every widget with an icon slot\n(`button.icon`, `iconButton.icon`, `floatingActionButton.icon`,\n`popupMenuButton.icon`, `rating.icon`, `offlineFallback.icon`,\n`permissionPrompt.icon`, …):\n\n1. **Name** — `\"home\"`, `\"folder_open\"`, … resolved through the\n   runtime's built-in icon table. Zero-cost, and the default reading of\n   a bare string.\n2. **Codepoint** — `{codepoint, fontFamily?, fontPackage?}` for glyphs\n   the name table does not carry.\n3. **`AssetRef`** — any form that primitive accepts (network URL,\n   `bundle://`, `assets/`, `data:image/svg+xml;…`, `client://`, or the\n   `{uri, origin?}` object). Which of those a runtime resolves is\n   declared, not assumed (`06_Runtime_Contract.md` §6.12).\n\nA bare string carrying a known scheme prefix (or an `assets/` path) is\nan asset; every other bare string is a **name**. That rule is what lets\nthe named form stay the zero-ceremony default while the same slot also\naccepts a server-served glyph.\n\nThis primitive exists so the rule is stated once. Before it, `icon`\ndocumented three forms while the eight other icon slots were typed as\nbare strings — so the same value was legal in one slot and undeclared\nin the next, and a codepoint object could not be written at all outside\nthe `icon` widget."},"LifecycleHooks":{"type":"object","properties":{"onInit":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onReady":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onMount":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onPause":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onResume":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onUnmount":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"},"onDestroy":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ActionOrList"}},"additionalProperties":false},"NavigationStyle":{"type":"object","properties":{"backgroundColor":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color"},"backgroundImage":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BackgroundImage"},"indicatorColor":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color","description":"Selection indicator pill color (rail / drawer / tabs)."},"indicatorShape":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BorderRadius","description":"Selection indicator corner radius. Defaults to a fully-rounded pill."},"dividerColor":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color","description":"Drawer-only — color of dividers between item groups."},"dividerThickness":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"dividerIndent":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension","description":"Drawer-only — leading inset before each divider."},"labelStyle":{"$ref":"#/$defs/TextStyle","description":"Default text style for item labels (selected and unselected). Per-item override via NavItem.style.labelStyle."},"iconStyle":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color"},"size":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Default icon color and size."},"selectedColor":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color","description":"Foreground color (icon + label) for the selected item."},"unselectedColor":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color","description":"Foreground color for non-selected items."},"elevation":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Visual styling for a navigation surface (drawer / rail / tabs /\nbottomBar). Every field is optional — omitted fields fall back to\nthe active theme's component defaults. Used by\n`NavigationConfig.style` (whole surface) and `NavItem.style`\n(per-item override).\n\nBackgrounds compose: `backgroundColor` paints first, then\n`backgroundImage` paints over it."},"Origin":{"type":"object","properties":{"connection":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\{\\{.*\\}\\}$"}],"description":"Outbound MCP client connection id, or a binding to one."}},"required":["connection"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Who serves a definition. Deliberately open so future sources need no new\nsyntax — today one shape is defined; `{ \"bundle\": ... }` / `{ \"agent\": ... }`\nand similar can be added without changing any document that uses it.\n\n`connection` names a live connection in the host's outbound MCP client\nregistry, addressed by the id used to open it. The DSL does not define how\nconnections are made — that is a host capability (`06_Runtime_Contract.md`\n§6.11.1); it defines only how a definition is addressed once one exists.\n\nA binding is the normal value here: an application opens its connections in\n`lifecycle.onInit` and keeps the ids in state.\n\nRuntimes MUST reject an Origin whose sole key they do not recognise rather\nthan falling back to the current origin — a permissive reading would render a\ndifferent server's UI under the requested one's identity (`07_Security.md`\n§7.10.1)."},"PermissionDeclaration":{"oneOf":[{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},{"enum":["readonly","interactive","full"]},{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"oneOf":[{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}]}}],"description":"Permissions per docs/08_Client_Extensions.md §8.4. Either a list of permission names, a profile shorthand, or an object grouped by category."},"RouteTransition":{"type":"object","properties":{"style":{"enum":["slide","fade","scale","cube","sharedAxis","fadeThrough"]},"duration":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension","description":"Total transition duration in milliseconds. Defaults to the M3 motion-system value for the chosen style."},"curve":{"$ref":"#/$defs/AnimationCurve","description":"Easing curve for the transition's progress. Defaults to `emphasized`."},"axis":{"enum":["horizontal","vertical"],"description":"Direction for `slide` / `sharedAxis`. Defaults to `horizontal`."},"reverse":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"When true, run the transition in reverse direction (for back navigation)."}},"required":["style"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Per-route page transition. Declared on a `RouteValue` so every\n`navigate` to that route uses the same transition, OR overridden\ninline on a `navigate` action. Six canonical styles:\n\n- `slide` — incoming page slides over the outgoing along the\n  direction (M3 default for forward navigation).\n- `fade` — cross-fade between pages at the same position.\n- `scale` — outgoing scales out, incoming scales in.\n- `cube` — perspective-rotate as if turning a 3D cube; needs a\n  perspective-aware compositor (falls back to `slide` when\n  unavailable).\n- `sharedAxis` — coordinated slide+fade across an axis (M3 motion\n  pattern for sibling-level navigation).\n- `fadeThrough` — outgoing fades out while incoming fades in\n  after a brief zero-opacity bridge (M3 motion pattern for\n  top-level navigation)."},"SemverLike":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+){0,2}(-[0-9A-Za-z.-]+)?$"},"StateBlock":{"type":"object","properties":{"initial":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"additionalProperties":false},"TextStyle":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\{\\{.*\\}\\}$","description":"Binding expression that resolves to a TextStyle object — typically `{{theme.typography.<role>}}`."},{"type":"object","properties":{"fontFamily":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}]},"fontSize":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"fontWeight":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^[1-9]00$","description":"CSS numeric spelling (`\"700\"`). Documents written against CSS habits use it, and the runtime reads it the same as the number."},{"enum":["thin","extraLight","light","normal","medium","semiBold","bold","extraBold","black","regular","w100","w200","w300","w400","w500","w600","w700","w800","w900"]},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}]},"fontStyle":{"oneOf":[{"enum":["normal","italic"]},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}]},"color":{"type":"string"},"backgroundColor":{"type":"string"},"letterSpacing":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"wordSpacing":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"height":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension","description":"Line-height multiplier — `height * fontSize` is the per-line vertical advance."},"decoration":{"oneOf":[{"enum":["none","underline","overline","lineThrough"]},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}]},"decorationColor":{"type":"string"},"decorationStyle":{"oneOf":[{"enum":["solid","double","dotted","dashed","wavy"]},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}]},"decorationThickness":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"fontFeatures":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"OpenType feature tags (`smcp`, `lnum`, `tnum`, `liga`, `dlig`, …)."},"shadows":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"object","properties":{"dx":{"type":"number"},"dy":{"type":"number"},"x":{"type":"number"},"y":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"`{dx, dy}` (canonical) or `{x, y}` (legacy alias) offset."},"blurRadius":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"}},"required":["color"],"additionalProperties":false}},"shader":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Gradient","description":"Gradient/shader fill applied to the rendered text via a shader mask. When set, `color` is ignored."}},"additionalProperties":true}],"description":"Inline text style applied per `text` widget instance. Layered on\ntop of an M3 typography role when `variant` is set, or used\nstandalone. Mirrors the theme `TextStyle` token shape (fontFamily,\nfontSize, fontWeight, lineHeight, letterSpacing, fontFeatureSettings)\nand adds the per-instance fields a content app needs: color,\ndecoration, shader (gradient fill), and shadow stack.\n\nThe object stays open. Documents in the field carry keys this style\nnever had — `textAlign` inside `style` is the common one, written by\nhand before it moved onto the widget — and the runtime simply ignores\nthem. Rejecting them here would not correct anything: validation runs\nwhen the document loads, so a stray key inside `style` would stop the\nwhole page instead of being ignored the way the runtime ignores it."},"ValidationConfig":{"oneOf":[{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"oneOf":[{"$ref":"#/$defs/ValidationRule"},{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ValidationRule"}}]}},{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ValidationRule"}}],"description":"Form validation per page. Shape A (object keyed by field) or Shape B (rule list)."},"ValidationRule":{"type":"object","properties":{"field":{"type":"string"},"type":{"type":"string"},"value":{},"message":{"type":"string"},"trigger":{"enum":["change","blur","submit"]}},"additionalProperties":true},"Widget":{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string"}},"required":["type"],"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Widget per docs/02_Widgets.md. Validated against the union in widgets.schema.json; left permissive here."}}}
